    "result_text": "All 50 tests across 36 test classes pass, with 0 failures and 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic from `(normalizedLastName, postcode)` and reworked the household semantics so `sharesHousehold` only bypasses the duplicate block.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`OwnerIdentity.householdId(lastName, postcode)`** \u2014 now hashes `normalizeName(lastName) + '|' + postcode` (SHA-256, first 12 hex chars) instead of `lastName + '|' + address`. A blank/absent postcode contributes `\"\"`.\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 assigns from `owner.getPostcode()` instead of address, so owners sharing lastName+postcode automatically get the same id (no lookup/link).\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount`** \u2014 unchanged; it already keys off the computed `householdId`, so the household-size input now derives from `(lastName, postcode)`.\n\n4. **`CheckIdentityUnique`** \u2014 the `identityKey` message now computes `householdId` from the postcode. The hard identity collision (same telephone+email) still fires regardless of `sharesHousehold` (this catches the full-duplicate case even when `sharesHousehold` is set).\n\n5. **New `CheckHouseholdUnique` step** (+ `DuplicateHouseholdException`, its handler, and escalation YAML) \u2014 wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `checkIdentityUnique`. It rejects a second owner sharing an existing owner's computed `householdId` with **409**, unless the request declares `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared household member.\n\n6. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a declared household member (`sharesHousehold: true`) is now left unflagged (`possibleDuplicate = false`), since a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\n\nThe key ordering that makes it all consistent: identity-collision check first (always 409 on exact identity match), then household-uniqueness (409 unless `sharesHousehold`), so `Cp28`'s shared-household exact-duplicate still 409s while `Cp10`/`Cp35` household duplicates 409 only without the declaration.",
